# haru-bf16.recipe -- Haru (the duplex speech model) served at bf16, the precision its release
# ships and its reference runs.
#
#   rad-convert <Haru checkpoint directory> \
#       --recipe data/recipes/haru-bf16.recipe -o haru-bf16.rad
#
# The real checkpoint is bf16 in every one of its 1022 tensors (checked against header.json), so
# this rule is exact there. It makes the serving precision explicit and gives a repacked f32
# checkpoint the same bf16 container. The LM's norms and PAD/EOP rows, the two audio projectors,
# the latent scale/bias and the MeanFlow head are declared f32 by their blocks; the loader widens
# those bf16 values to f32 exactly (core/build/rad_builder.cpp:207-227), so they stay f32 in the
# container. The codec is declared at the config's dtype, bfloat16.

*                                    cast dtype=bf16
